# AUTHORED-BY Claude Opus 5.5
#
# Machine-readable normative-statement companion for "Solid Storage Service Description"
# (index.html in this directory). COMPLEMENTARY: the full-text spec is the normative document;
# this graph enumerates its normative statements so conformance suites and coverage gates can
# consume them. Format: the jeswr/spec-companion model (spec: requirement markup + the
# E / A-int / A-exist / P testability spine + per-statement test-case links or honest gaps).
# Statement texts are verbatim quotes of index.html (tags stripped, entities decoded, [[refs]]
# unbracketed, whitespace collapsed); tools/spec-check checks the quotes, anchors, levels and
# that every normative paragraph is listed.
#
# Testability:
#   E       deterministically black-box testable (a document or request/response decides it).
#   A-int   a non-interference or uniformity property: samplable, not exhaustively decidable.
#   A-exist audit or inspection only.
#   P       not testable as specified.
# Graph-shape statements link the invalid vectors in examples/invalid/ that the SHACL shapes
# reject; protocol statements carry a test gap until the storage-conformance suite covers them.

@base <https://jeswr.github.io/solid-specs/specs/service-description/spec.statements.ttl> .
@prefix sc:      <https://w3id.org/jeswr/spec-companion#> .
@prefix spec:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/spec#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<> a sc:CompanionDocument ;
    dcterms:title "Solid Storage Service Description normative-statement companion"@en ;
    sc:companionOf <https://jeswr.github.io/solid-specs/specs/service-description/> ;
    sc:specVersion "2026-10-26" ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-26"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://jeswr.org/#me> ;
    dcterms:description "Extracted with AI assistance (Claude Opus 5.5, Anthropic) from the spec source in the same commit; awaiting review by the human editor, like the spec itself."@en .

